meta {
  name: 63 Print Templates E2E
  seq: 70
}

docs {
  # Print Templates — end-to-end substitution check

  Creates one **checklist-style** PDF template per print type used across the
  app, then proves the `{placeholder}` engine replaces every variable — first
  with controlled dummy data (`generate`), then against a real record (the
  production print endpoints). Every response is a **binary PDF**; in Bruno use
  the response panel's PDF preview (or *Save Response → Save to file*) to eyeball
  each value.

  ## Renderer syntax (custom engine — NOT Handlebars/Mustache)
  - `{placeholder}`  — single value from `variables` (single brace; `{{x}}`
    would render as `{value}`, so scalars are always single-brace).
  - `{{#each key}}…{{/each}}` — one block per row in `sections[key]`; inside,
    `{col}` (or `{{this.col}}`) resolves the row's fields.
  - `{{image:ID}}` — `<img>` from `images[ID]`.
  - `<signing_authority_tag>…</signing_authority_tag>` — footer block expanded
    once per entry in `signatories` (`{name}`, `{designation}`,
    `{registrationNumber}`, `{signatureImage}`).

  ## Run order
  1. **Business Auth → Login** (captures `businessAccessToken`).
  2. For each type: run **Create** (captures `<type>TemplateId`), then
     **Generate (dummy)**, then **Print (real)**.

  ## Types & endpoints covered
  | Type | Create → | Real print endpoint |
  | ---- | -------- | ------------------- |
  | order_print | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /orders/{{orderId}}/print` `{type:"order_print"}` |
  | lab_report | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/print` `{type:"lab_report"}` |
  | lab_all_report | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/print-all` |
  | lab_panel | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/print` `{type:"lab_panel"}` |
  | order_label_print | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /accession/samples/print-label` `{sampleId}` |
  | multiple_order_label_print | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /accession/samples/print-labels` `{ids}` |
  | bill_print | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /orders/{{orderId}}/print` `{type:"bill_print"}` |
  | trf_print | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /orders/{{orderId}}/print` `{type:"trf_print"}` |
  | lab_quotation_print | `POST /pdf-report-templates` | `POST /orders/{{orderId}}/print` `{type:"lab_quotation_print"}` |

  ## Notes
  - The real-print requests always pass an explicit `templateId`. If omitted, the
    backend falls back to the tenant's *single* active template of that type and
    throws `AmbiguousPrintTemplateException` when more than one exists — and these
    Create requests add active templates, so pass the id.
  - The real-print requests need existing records: `{{orderId}}` (with items /
    payments / a matching status), `{{labReportId}}`, and `{{sampleId}}`. Seed
    them via the Orders / Technician Reporting / Accession flows first.
}
